      "days_before_request": 0,
      "body": "75F on CAPD, hospital day 6. Infectious source remains the obstructing R ureteral stone — decompression again discussed this AM, pt still undecided and has not consented, so the source has not been controlled. T 38.1, HR 86, BP 126/72, MAP ~90 without any vasopressors at any point this admission; not in shock. Lactate 1.9. Alert, no encephalopathy. WBC 10.9, CRP 249, K 4.6, Hgb 8.4, Cr 9.63. Urine cx 4/22: E. faecalis (ampicillin S, vancomycin S). Allergy list re-verified face-to-face today: latex (mild contact dermatitis) is the only entry — pt again confirms she has no penicillin allergy and no beta-lactam allergy of any kind. PD effluent clear, exchanges tolerated, UF adequate. Code status full. Copy-forward: remote L wrist ORIF 2021, healed, no residual issues. Family meeting planned, daughter to join by phone."
